    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "The task is fully scaffolded into three steps. In part a, the student subtracts the right short side from the left side, (x+4)-3, to find the missing vertical side. In part b, they add all six sides, collecting x terms and constants. In part c, they take out the HCF of 2. There are no hidden decisions and no unsignposted insight. The hardest demand is reading the missing length from the rectilinear shape, which is a small representation step. This is slightly above p15-q11, which has a single factorising step with the rectangle's length given. It is clearly below the open-ended listing and comparison in A4, and below p14-q9, where students must find missing lengths unprompted across several shapes.",
